<title>CANADA: NatBank Canada '96 loan loss provision falls.</title>
<headline>NatBank Canada '96 loan loss provision falls.</headline>
<dateline>MONTREAL 1996-12-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Bank of Canada said on Thursday its provision for loan losses fell to C$43.8 million in the fourth quarter ended October 31, down from C$66.3 million in the same period a year earlier.</p>
<p>National Bank said in a statement its full-year provision dropped to C$235 million in 1996, down from C$215 million in 1995.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
